Task: Car-following, texel-snapped shadow camera (FR7). Changes: scene.ts gains SUN_SHADOW_TEXEL + sunShadowSnap (pure, red-first - 3 tests: idempotent, sub-cell creep leaves the map still, followSun aims light+target at the snapped focus) and GameScene.followSun; the sun light+target now travel with the car instead of holding fixed +-8 bounds around the world origin, so both loops keep full shadows and the 1024 map stays sharp on the window, not the town. main.ts wires followSun(motor.position) into tickVehicle. The snap rounds on the map's own lattice but solves the rounding step BACK IN THE GROUND PLANE (the 2x2 determinant SNAP_GROUND_DET) - the first cut rebuilt the focus in the light basis and dropped its y, so the x/z round trip drifted ~0.002 and idempotence failed; ground-plane steps keep the focus a real ground point and the lattice exact. 3 files. Coverage: scene.test.ts 8 tests (3 red-first for FR7). Why: FR7 - a creeping car must never slide the shadow map between cells (that is the shimmer), and a growing town must never lose its shadows at the edges.
